export anchor SignageStyle:
    number: 22
    screen: ProjectsDashboard
    name: Signage
    idea: Wayfinding signage for work, with huge high-contrast type, black and safety-yellow bands, big pictograms and numbered sections that read from across the room.
    base: light
    palette:
        white: #ffffff, the page and section ground
        black: #111111, text, rules, the top band, the primary button and this week's bars
        safetyYellow: #ffcc00, the greeting band, the active nav item, At risk and the focus halo
        goGreen: #00703c with white, the On track pictogram and word
        stopRed: #c8102e with white, the Behind pictogram and word
        midGrey: #8c8c8c, last week's chart bars only
        lightGrey: #e6e6e6, the meter track
        muted: #444444, placeholder text
    type:
        Helvetica Neue, Helvetica, Arial Nova, Arial, Liberation Sans,
        sans-serif, heavy and mostly uppercase. Summary numbers are up to
        128px at weight 900 with tight tracking, the greeting up to 96px
        uppercase, section titles up to 56px uppercase, project names up to
        40px, activity text 24px and labels 20px weight 800 uppercase with
        0.04em tracking. Sizes scale down with clamp on phones.
    layout:
        Full width stacked bands, no columns. A black top band holds a
        yellow square B mark, uppercase nav words with the current one on
        yellow, a white search block, a square bell and the avatar. A
        yellow band carries a black circle badge, the greeting, the date
        with a black 4 TASKS OVERDUE tag and a big black New project
        button. Then four giant counts split by thick black rules, with the
        overdue count reversed to yellow on black. Numbered sections follow
        like platform signs, 1 Projects as one full width row per project
        with a pictogram tile, name, status word, facts and a giant
        percent over a thick meter, 2 Tasks done with week totals beside
        large bars, and 3 Latest as a departure board of times and events.
        A hazard stripe ends the dashboard. Phones stack each row.
    spacing: An 8px unit in big steps. 24px row padding, 48px section padding and a 40px page gutter.
    density: Very low. One project per full width row and one fact per line.
    corners: Square everywhere, except 6px on pictogram tiles and section number blocks and a full circle on the badge.
    borders: Heavy black rules, 8px between bands, 4px between rows and cells and 3px in the style sheet tables.
    shadows: None.
    icons:
        Big solid pictograms in 88px tiles, a ringed tick on green for On
        track, a solid triangle with an exclamation mark on yellow inside a
        black edge for At risk and a boxed cross on red for Behind. Section
        numbers sit in 72px black squares. Arrows mark links.
    focus: A 6px black outline with a 12px yellow halo. On the black band a 6px yellow outline.
    tone: Extremely direct uppercase, such as 4 OVERDUE, TASKS DONE, LATEST and ALL PROJECTS with an arrow.
